    source: "---\ntitle: Learning Journal\ndate: 2024-07-04\nsummary: Go\ntags: [go, golang, programming, journal]\ncover: https://go.dev/images/go-logo-white.svg\ndraft: false\n---\n\nMy backlog of links to documentation, training material, and videos I used to learn go.\n\n#### 04 Jul 24\n---\n\n``17:33`` - [``Beginners Should Think Differently When Writing Golang``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PyDMqgOkiR8)\n\n``17:37`` - [``This Will Make Everyone Understand Golang Interfaces``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rH0bpx7I2Dk)\n\n``20:44`` - [``Go Pointers: When & How To Use Them Efficiently``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3WsEDZRif6U)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n#### 05 Jul 24\n---\n\n``15:06`` - [``A Tour of Go - Pointer receivers``](https://go.dev/tour/methods/4)\n\n``15:30`` - [``go.dev Call your code from another module``](https://go.dev/doc/tutorial/call-module-code)\n\n``16:30`` - [``[Gist] ayoubzulfiqar - The Folder Structure for Every Golang Project``](https://gist.github.com/ayoubzulfiqar/9f1a34049332711fddd4d4b2bfd46096)\n\n``16:46`` - [``anthdm - How To Build A Chat And Data Feed With WebSockets In Golang?``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JuUAEYLkGbM)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n#### 07 Jul 24\n---\n\n``15:06`` - [``Go by Example: Structs``](https://gobyexample.com/structs)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n#### 07 Jul 24\n---\n\n``14:00`` - [``anthdm - How To Build A Custom TCP Server In Golang!?``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qJQrrscB1-4)\n\n``17:00`` - [``Rob Pike - Go proverbs``](https://go-proverbs.github.io/)\n\n``21:40`` - [``Rob Pike - Concurrency is not Parallelism by Rob Pike``](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oV9rvDllKEg)\n\nNotes:\n\nConcurrency: The composition of independently executing processes (things)\n- Concurrency is about dealing with alot of things at once\n\nParallelism: The simultaneous execution of multiple things (possibly related, possibly not)\n- Parallelism is about doing alot of things at once\n\n``21:40`` - [``Communicating Sequential Processes by C.A.R. Hoare``](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~crary/819-f09/Hoare78.pdf)\n",
